</blockquote>
<p>This, uh&#8230; actually made it kind of worse? My point is that the SCP doesn't display any indication that would make an outside observer believe that these listed precautions are necessary. This individual is inherently very much average, and even if they <em>were</em> accosted by a member of a GOI, I don't see why the Foundation would need to be so preemptively concerned. Even if this individual joined a GOI (what would they have to offer to said GOI anyway?), the best course of action would be to keep them either sedated around the clock or simply amnesticized and provided with a cover story.</p>
<p>Also, a containment breach alarm usually would result in staff evacuations and security dispatch. Neither of these seem a necessary response for the scenario that's meant to trigger the alarm in this case.</p>

